                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_13\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit's diff (in TableFactoryRenderer.java) changes the generated factory-method call:\n\n    return Table.of(t, name, namespace, Triggers.getAllTriggers(t, sharedTriggers, triggers));\n\nto:\n\n    return Table.of(t, namespace, name, Triggers.getAllTriggers(t, sharedTriggers, triggers));\n\ni.e. it swaps the \"name\" (table name) and \"namespace\" arguments, matching them to the actual\ngenerated static factory method signature `of(Transaction t, Namespace namespace, String tableName, ...)`\n(the \"namespace\" parameter is declared before the \"tableName\"/\"name\" parameter in the generated\nTable classes' `of(...)` and constructor signatures, as seen throughout TableRenderer.java's generated\ncode, e.g. `static XTable of(Transaction t, Namespace namespace, String tableName, ...)`).\n\nSearching the candidates for the buggy call pattern `t, name, namespace` shows it appears in three\ncandidates: candidate_13, candidate_16, and candidate_23. Since the candidates are ordered\nchronologically, candidate_13 is the earliest occurrence and is where this line was first\nintroduced (it is part of a larger commit that added Namespace support to TableFactoryRenderer,\nTableRenderer, and Schema.java, introducing the `defaultNamespace`/`namespace` field and updating\nthe `of(...)` factory/constructor signatures to take `Namespace namespace` before the table name).\nIn that same commit, the generated call to the per-table `of(...)` factory method was written with\nthe arguments in the wrong order (`t, name, namespace` instead of `t, namespace, name`), which is\nexactly the bug later corrected by the fix commit. Candidate_16 and candidate_23 merely\ncarry/refactor this pre-existing line (candidate_16 just changes `_(...)` calls to `line(...)` calls\nwithout altering argument order; candidate_23 is effectively the fix itself, correcting the order).\n\nTherefore candidate_13 is the commit that introduced the argument-ordering bug described in the fix\ncommit message (\"fixed generated table factory method argument ordering\").\n"
